.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt BN_NEW 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm BN_new ,
.Nm BN_secure_new ,
.Nm BN_clear ,
.Nm BN_free ,
.Nm BN_clear_free
.Nd allocate and free BIGNUMs
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/bn.h
.Ft BIGNUM *
.Fo BN_new
.Fa void
.Fc
.Ft BIGNUM *
.Fo BN_secure_new
.Fa void
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo BN_clear
.Fa "BIGNUM *a"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo BN_free
.Fa "BIGNUM *a"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo BN_clear_free
.Fa "BIGNUM *a"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn BN_new
allocates and initializes a
.Vt BIGNUM
structure.
.Fn BN_secure_new
does the same except that the secure heap
.Xr OPENSSL_secure_malloc 3
is used to store the value.
.Pp
.Fn BN_clear
is used to destroy sensitive data such as keys when they are no longer
needed.
It erases the memory used by
.Fa a
and sets it to the value 0. If
.Fa a
is NULL, nothing is done.
.Pp
.Fn BN_free
frees the components of the
.Vt BIGNUM ,
and if it was created by
.Fn BN_new ,
also the structure itself.
.Fn BN_clear_free
additionally overwrites the data before the memory is returned to the
system.
If
.Fa a
is NULL, nothing is done.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn BN_new
and
.Fn BN_secure_new
return a pointer to the
.Vt BIGNUM
initialised to the value 0. If the allocation fails, they return
.Dv NULL
and set an error code that can be obtained by
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 .
.Pp
.Fn BN_clear ,
.Fn BN_free
and
.Fn BN_clear_free
have no return values.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 ,
.Xr OPENSSL_secure_malloc 3
.Sh HISTORY
.Xr BN_init 3
was removed in OpenSSL 1.1.0; use
.Fn BN_new
instead.
